1
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:12,560
This is Momo.

2
00:00:12,610 --> 00:00:13,900
This is a teddy bear.

3
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:14,830
Two eyes.

4
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:15,790
Soft fur.

5
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:16,810
One is living.

6
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:17,880
One is not.

7
00:00:17,912 --> 00:00:18,572
Easy?

8
00:00:18,632 --> 00:00:20,722
Then try the six things in our box.

9
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,539
First, a practice round.

10
00:00:22,569 --> 00:00:23,529
The teddy bear.

11
00:00:23,579 --> 00:00:24,869
Point left for living.

12
00:00:24,899 --> 00:00:26,409
Point right for non-living.

13
00:00:26,479 --> 00:00:27,129
Go!

14
00:00:32,587 --> 00:00:33,487
Locked in!

15
00:00:33,548 --> 00:00:34,598
Non-living.

16
00:00:34,758 --> 00:00:36,058
It never eats.

17
00:00:36,053 --> 00:00:36,863
Non-living!

18
00:00:36,953 --> 00:00:38,223
It's full of cotton.

19
00:00:38,222 --> 00:00:40,042
But it has eyes and fur like me.

20
00:00:40,032 --> 00:00:41,412
Why isn't it living?

21
00:00:41,537 --> 00:00:43,637
The teddy bear is a non-living thing.

22
00:00:43,697 --> 00:00:45,727
Eyes and fur are only how it looks.

23
00:00:45,767 --> 00:00:47,157
We need better clues.

24
00:00:47,536 --> 00:00:48,646
Here is the game.

25
00:00:48,706 --> 00:00:50,216
It's You against the Buddies.

26
00:00:50,266 --> 00:00:51,456
You lock in first.

27
00:00:51,496 --> 00:00:53,626
Then Pip, Basil and Momo answer.

28
00:00:53,687 --> 00:00:56,457
Every time you are right, put up one finger on your other

29
00:00:56,207 --> 00:00:56,847
hand.

30
00:00:56,897 --> 00:00:58,247
Five fingers wins.

31
00:00:58,307 --> 00:00:59,947
No lock-in, no point.

32
00:00:59,997 --> 00:01:02,247
And a cicak is hiding in this video.

33
00:01:02,297 --> 00:01:03,117
Find it!

34
00:01:03,309 --> 00:01:07,569
Today you will learn what diversity means, how to classify things into

35
00:01:07,319 --> 00:01:10,829
groups, and how to tell living things from non-living things.

36
00:01:11,461 --> 00:01:13,121
Our six things came from here.

37
00:01:13,181 --> 00:01:15,491
A void deck and a garden in Toa Payoh.

38
00:01:15,551 --> 00:01:16,501
Look around.

39
00:01:16,557 --> 00:01:17,247
A mynah.

40
00:01:17,367 --> 00:01:18,067
Ants.

41
00:01:18,107 --> 00:01:19,227
A papaya tree.

42
00:01:19,277 --> 00:01:20,077
A bench.

43
00:01:20,127 --> 00:01:21,057
A bicycle.

44
00:01:21,107 --> 00:01:22,527
A blue recycling bin.

45
00:01:22,587 --> 00:01:23,977
So many different things!

46
00:01:24,424 --> 00:01:28,154
There is a great variety of living and non-living things around us.

47
00:01:28,204 --> 00:01:29,734
This is called diversity.

48
00:01:30,366 --> 00:01:31,196
So many!

49
00:01:31,196 --> 00:01:32,476
How do we keep track?

50
00:01:32,439 --> 00:01:33,769
We put them into groups.

51
00:01:33,829 --> 00:01:35,159
Let's start with six.

52
00:01:35,651 --> 00:01:36,571
Are you ready?

53
00:01:36,991 --> 00:01:37,751
Three!

54
00:01:38,141 --> 00:01:38,781
Two!

55
00:01:39,151 --> 00:01:39,781
One!

56
00:01:40,181 --> 00:01:40,851
Go!

57
00:01:41,467 --> 00:01:42,247
Day one.

58
00:01:42,307 --> 00:01:43,827
Six things, one box.

59
00:01:43,857 --> 00:01:46,077
The lid has holes, so air can get in.

60
00:01:46,117 --> 00:01:49,527
The mealworm has oats to eat and a juicy carrot for water.

61
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:52,107
The plant gets water, and light from the window.

62
00:01:53,558 --> 00:01:54,388
Round one.

63
00:01:54,448 --> 00:01:55,848
The wind-up robot.

64
00:01:55,898 --> 00:01:56,908
Look at it go!

65
00:01:56,968 --> 00:01:58,258
Point left for living.

66
00:01:58,288 --> 00:01:59,828
Point right for non-living.

67
00:02:05,286 --> 00:02:06,186
Locked in!

68
00:02:06,247 --> 00:02:06,917
Living!

69
00:02:06,997 --> 00:02:08,397
It moves, so it's living!

70
00:02:08,392 --> 00:02:09,432
Non-living.

71
00:02:09,582 --> 00:02:11,462
I saw you wind it up, Basil.

72
00:02:11,459 --> 00:02:12,409
Non-living.

73
00:02:12,459 --> 00:02:13,949
Does it ever get hungry?

74
00:02:14,373 --> 00:02:14,981
Watch.

75
00:02:14,794 --> 00:02:16,033
The robot stops.

76
00:02:15,846 --> 00:02:18,055
A spring inside was pushing it.

77
00:02:18,205 --> 00:02:20,585
Nobody winds it up, so it stays still.

78
00:02:20,635 --> 00:02:21,515
All night.

79
00:02:21,565 --> 00:02:22,655
All of day two.

80
00:02:22,962 --> 00:02:25,172
It does not need water, food or air.

81
00:02:25,232 --> 00:02:26,372
It does not grow.

82
00:02:26,412 --> 00:02:28,962
The wind-up robot is a non-living thing.

83
00:02:29,457 --> 00:02:30,447
Pointed right?

84
00:02:30,487 --> 00:02:31,577
One finger up!

85
00:02:31,639 --> 00:02:32,019
Aww.

86
00:02:32,329 --> 00:02:33,839
So moving is not the clue!

87
00:02:33,833 --> 00:02:36,613
Then is a thing that stays still always non-living?

88
00:02:37,936 --> 00:02:38,796
Round two.

89
00:02:38,846 --> 00:02:39,676
Day two.

90
00:02:39,726 --> 00:02:40,766
The green bean.

91
00:02:40,836 --> 00:02:41,826
It is a seed.

92
00:02:41,896 --> 00:02:43,216
It has not moved at all.

93
00:02:43,296 --> 00:02:44,776
Living, or non-living?

94
00:02:44,826 --> 00:02:45,546
Point!

95
00:02:51,015 --> 00:02:51,915
Locked in!

96
00:02:51,976 --> 00:02:53,016
Non-living.

97
00:02:53,156 --> 00:02:54,966
I watched it for one whole day.

98
00:02:55,106 --> 00:02:56,246
It did nothing.

99
00:02:56,249 --> 00:02:56,999
Living!

100
00:02:57,069 --> 00:02:58,579
It's green, like a leaf.

101
00:02:58,577 --> 00:02:59,247
Living!

102
00:02:59,317 --> 00:03:01,097
Taugeh grows from green beans.

103
00:03:01,117 --> 00:03:02,207
I eat taugeh!

104
00:03:02,513 --> 00:03:04,173
Three buddies, two answers.

105
00:03:04,223 --> 00:03:05,763
Let's shrink down and watch.

106
00:03:05,823 --> 00:03:06,633
Quietly.

107
00:03:09,925 --> 00:03:11,135
You are tiny now.

108
00:03:11,415 --> 00:03:13,655
The green bean is as big as a bus.

109
00:03:14,781 --> 00:03:15,571
Listen.

110
00:03:19,019 --> 00:03:20,269
The skin splits.

111
00:03:20,549 --> 00:03:21,969
A root pushes out.

112
00:03:24,079 --> 00:03:25,589
Nobody wound it up.

113
00:03:25,879 --> 00:03:27,209
Nobody pushed it.

114
00:03:27,479 --> 00:03:29,249
It is growing by itself.

115
00:03:31,456 --> 00:03:33,326
The green bean is a living thing.

116
00:03:33,396 --> 00:03:34,766
It was living all along.

117
00:03:34,826 --> 00:03:35,876
It took in water.

118
00:03:35,936 --> 00:03:37,296
Then it began to grow.

119
00:03:37,853 --> 00:03:38,893
Pointed left?

120
00:03:38,943 --> 00:03:40,033
One finger up!

121
00:03:40,091 --> 00:03:41,231
I was careful.

122
00:03:41,401 --> 00:03:43,291
But I did not watch long enough.

123
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:44,917
Momo, living is right.

124
00:03:44,947 --> 00:03:46,797
But green is only how it looks.

125
00:03:46,857 --> 00:03:48,707
A green pencil is non-living.

126
00:03:48,714 --> 00:03:50,024
No point for me!

127
00:03:50,024 --> 00:03:51,424
So what ARE the clues?

128
00:03:51,852 --> 00:03:52,982
Not how it looks.

129
00:03:53,042 --> 00:03:54,252
Not whether it moves.

130
00:03:54,322 --> 00:03:55,432
Ask two things.

131
00:03:55,492 --> 00:03:56,452
What does it need?

132
00:03:56,552 --> 00:03:57,522
What can it do?

133
00:03:57,889 --> 00:04:00,269
Living things need water, food and air.

134
00:04:00,319 --> 00:04:03,669
Living things grow, respond to changes and reproduce.

135
00:04:03,739 --> 00:04:06,069
You will test these in the next two episodes.

136
00:04:07,117 --> 00:04:08,417
Does it move?

137
00:04:08,617 --> 00:04:09,917
That's NOT the clue!

138
00:04:10,117 --> 00:04:11,417
What does it NEED?

139
00:04:11,617 --> 00:04:12,917
What can it DO?

140
00:04:14,293 --> 00:04:15,133
Day ten.

141
00:04:15,193 --> 00:04:19,273
Time to sort all six into two groups: living things and non-living

142
00:04:19,023 --> 00:04:19,663
things.

143
00:04:19,723 --> 00:04:21,153
Momo, you go first.

144
00:04:21,657 --> 00:04:22,397
Squish...

145
00:04:22,587 --> 00:04:23,287
squish...

146
00:04:23,457 --> 00:04:24,537
knock, knock.

147
00:04:24,527 --> 00:04:25,327
Done!

148
00:04:25,675 --> 00:04:27,115
Something is not right.

149
00:04:27,165 --> 00:04:29,155
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

150
00:04:29,215 --> 00:04:30,055
Hold on!

151
00:04:35,569 --> 00:04:36,619
Arms crossed?

152
00:04:36,669 --> 00:04:37,709
One finger up!

153
00:04:37,789 --> 00:04:38,409
Look.

154
00:04:38,479 --> 00:04:40,549
The teddy bear is sitting with the mealworm.

155
00:04:40,599 --> 00:04:42,559
Momo sorted by soft and hard.

156
00:04:42,633 --> 00:04:44,323
I wanted to know how they feel!

157
00:04:44,333 --> 00:04:45,253
Good sort.

158
00:04:45,303 --> 00:04:46,503
Wrong question.

159
00:04:46,933 --> 00:04:48,873
Momo did put things into groups.

160
00:04:48,933 --> 00:04:50,263
Alike things together.

161
00:04:50,283 --> 00:04:51,703
Different things apart.

162
00:04:52,010 --> 00:04:56,800
Classification is the grouping of things based on their similarities and differences.

163
00:04:57,492 --> 00:04:59,092
You can choose soft or hard.

164
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:01,612
But our question is living or non-living.

165
00:05:01,662 --> 00:05:03,202
So we use the real clues.

166
00:05:03,252 --> 00:05:04,632
Has anyone done that?

167
00:05:06,277 --> 00:05:07,897
My homework from Day one.

168
00:05:08,037 --> 00:05:10,377
I fixed the green bean after Round two.

169
00:05:10,442 --> 00:05:11,292
Showdown!

170
00:05:11,332 --> 00:05:12,392
Double points.

171
00:05:12,432 --> 00:05:14,402
Pip made a table with two columns.

172
00:05:14,452 --> 00:05:16,322
One thing is still in the wrong column.

173
00:05:16,389 --> 00:05:18,359
Is it one, the wind-up robot?

174
00:05:18,409 --> 00:05:19,399
Two, the plant?

175
00:05:19,459 --> 00:05:20,689
Or three, the pebble?

176
00:05:20,749 --> 00:05:22,099
Show me with your fingers.

177
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:29,460
Locked in!

178
00:05:29,521 --> 00:05:30,111
Two!

179
00:05:30,141 --> 00:05:31,341
We water that plant.

180
00:05:31,291 --> 00:05:32,361
It needs water.

181
00:05:32,358 --> 00:05:33,108
Two!

182
00:05:33,098 --> 00:05:34,418
I saw a new leaf.

183
00:05:34,418 --> 00:05:36,338
But it never moved out of its pot!

184
00:05:36,774 --> 00:05:39,414
Watch the plant, from day one to day fourteen.

185
00:05:39,474 --> 00:05:40,784
It stays in its pot.

186
00:05:40,814 --> 00:05:42,094
But it has a new leaf.

187
00:05:42,154 --> 00:05:44,324
And it grows towards the light from the window.

188
00:05:44,364 --> 00:05:46,044
The plant is a living thing.

189
00:05:47,109 --> 00:05:47,699
Fixed!

190
00:05:47,449 --> 00:05:49,879
A plant stays in one place.

191
00:05:49,969 --> 00:05:51,639
But it is a living thing.

192
00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:52,620
Two fingers?

193
00:05:52,670 --> 00:05:54,410
Put up two more on your score hand!

194
00:05:54,857 --> 00:05:56,127
Pip used a table.

195
00:05:56,167 --> 00:05:58,777
The same two groups can be shown in other ways too.

196
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:03,605
We can present our classification using pictures, a table, and a graphic

197
00:06:03,355 --> 00:06:04,225
organiser.

198
00:06:06,161 --> 00:06:07,061
Day thirty.

199
00:06:07,121 --> 00:06:08,411
What is under the cloth?

200
00:06:10,724 --> 00:06:12,804
The green bean is a tall plant now.

201
00:06:12,854 --> 00:06:14,154
The mealworm is bigger.

202
00:06:14,204 --> 00:06:15,704
The plant has new leaves.

203
00:06:15,754 --> 00:06:18,124
And the teddy bear, the robot and the pebble?

204
00:06:18,184 --> 00:06:19,474
Exactly the same.

205
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:21,228
Three living things.

206
00:06:21,278 --> 00:06:22,638
Three non-living things.

207
00:06:22,729 --> 00:06:24,029
Does it move?

208
00:06:24,229 --> 00:06:25,529
That's NOT the clue!

209
00:06:25,729 --> 00:06:27,029
What does it NEED?

210
00:06:27,229 --> 00:06:28,529
What can it DO?

211
00:06:29,619 --> 00:06:30,949
Show me your score hand!

212
00:06:31,009 --> 00:06:32,029
More than three?

213
00:06:32,079 --> 00:06:33,259
You beat the Buddies.

214
00:06:33,299 --> 00:06:34,359
Five fingers?

215
00:06:34,419 --> 00:06:35,339
High five!

216
00:06:35,712 --> 00:06:37,202
Did you spot the cicak?

217
00:06:37,252 --> 00:06:39,462
It was on the window frame on day fourteen.

218
00:06:39,512 --> 00:06:41,502
Is a cicak living or non-living?

219
00:06:41,552 --> 00:06:42,762
Tell someone at home.

220
00:06:44,350 --> 00:06:45,050
Oh no.

221
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:46,290
Is it sad?

222
00:06:46,347 --> 00:06:47,967
A drooping plant isn't sad.

223
00:06:48,027 --> 00:06:48,987
What does it need?

224
00:06:49,087 --> 00:06:50,907
Lock in your answer for next time.

225
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:52,250
Now you know!
